Z||000000||FieroGTGirl||07-04-2000||12:54 AM||||OK Fellow Washingtonians...Isn't it amazing there are NO clouds at the coast?! Took this pic a couple of weekends ago...<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Scanned_Picture_2.JPG">  <P>The ocean and the mountains in one pic.  We are truely lucky to live in such a beautiful place.  We got it all, the ocean, mountains, rain forest, and desert.  What more could someone want?<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Scanned_Picture_1.JPG">  <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Kristina_1.JPG">  <p>[This message has been edited by FieroGTGirl (edited 07-04-2000).]||||reg||7
Z||000001||Phaeton||07-04-2000||04:58 AM||||Snow and tundra come to mind.<P>Think about it.<BR>Eight months of no insects or crawlies of ANY kind.  Laying flat in the snow watching the northern lights.  Snow berms by the roads to bounce Fiero's back between the lines.<P>I spent some years in western Washington with my grandparents and am awed to this day thinking of the greenery of the rain forest/ocean areas.  A friendly jungle.||||reg||12
Z||000002||Old Lar||07-04-2000||06:58 AM||||Love the ocean shots.  However this one was one of the prettiest ocean mountain shots I have. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Anaholabeach.jpg"> <P>I wish I lived nearby. It is Anahola Beach on the island of Kauai.  Taken when I had the chance to go to Kauai in 1990.||||reg||14
